Where to Put Your Service Offer

Location	                     Format	                                     Length
LinkedIn headline	One sentence: "Python automation for [client type]"	    Under 120 characters
Portfolio site hero	       Header + one sentence + call to action button	Under 20 words
GitHub profile README	   Two to three bullet points listing specific services	Under 50 words
Proposal or outreach message	Full offer: client, problem, outcome, tools, proof	One paragraph
Upwork or freelance platform profile	First 300 characters must carry the core offer	Start with the outcome

Tip: Write your service offer in the second-person perspective on your portfolio site and in the first-person perspective in outreach messages. "You need X, I deliver Y" works for a landing page. "I help clients who need X by delivering Y" works in a direct message or proposal.

Note: The formula works for any local market. "I help Jua Kali workshops that lose track of pending jobs by building a simple Python job tracker they can run on any laptop" is a complete service offer. "I help dairy cooperatives that record milk yields by hand by automating their weekly report into a one-click script" is another. Same structure. Different domain. Start with the client you already know.